course: dictionary
lesson: 13128
title: Foliage, the leaves together
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Foliage is a word for leaves, but for lots of them all together. One leaf is not foliage. A whole tree's leaves, or a bush's leaves, make foliage. You can use it for plants and for many trees.
explain: «The fox crept under the thick foliage, where no one could see it.» The clues are thick and hidden. Thick things are full and crowded, and a fox hides in things that are full of leaves. So foliage must mean the leaves of plants and trees.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence. Swap in «the leaves of plants» for foliage: «The fox crept under the thick leaves of plants, where no one could see it.» It still makes sense, so your meaning is right.
fact: Foliage means the leaves of a plant or many trees, all together.
fact: Foliage is uncountable, so you do not say «a foliage» or «foliages». Say «some foliage» or «thick foliage».
fact: «Green foliage covered the old wall.» Here the green leaves cover the wall all together.
fact: In autumn, the foliage in Canada and New England turns red and gold.
fact: In art, artists draw foliage with light and dark greens.
exercise: «The deer hid in the thick foliage.» What is foliage here? | A path for walking | A stream running through the forest | The soft brown earth under a tree | *The leaves of plants and trees
exercise: Find the word in «Green foliage covered the old wall.» that names the leaves together. | Green | wall | covered | *foliage
exercise: Which is correct for leaves all together? | foliages | a foliage | *some foliage | many foliages
test: «The birds sang high in the green foliage.» What does foliage mean? | Tall, thin trunks | The sky above the trees | The birds' nests | *The leaves of plants and trees
test: In art lessons, which colours do artists often use to draw foliage? | *Light and dark greens | Bright purple only | Black and white only | Pink and orange only
exam: In the forest, the animals were hidden by thick foliage. What does foliage mean? | A thin cloud | A hard stone | *The green leaves of plants and trees | The dark night
